  "details": "This is basically for easy moderation and more complex world creation, that way any admin or mod of the group in a group public instance can automatically moderate bouncer style or in any other way world creators choose to. Maybe even make it so only members of the group can enter and the rest are in a waiting/verification area.\n\nHere's an example of where this might be useful:\n\nI am active in a world that has a bouncer system. I tend to crash a lot though, and any time I crash and re-join I have to be re-verified in the same instance.\n\nLetting a world read the group hosting and the status of people in it will make it so creators can set group members as automatically verified, as well as group admins to automatically be bouncers or have extra permissions such as projecting their voice and so on.\n\nThis also lets the instance still have public access and exposure, while maintaining the safety of a group only or group+ instance.\n\nTL;DR: Allow worlds to read the group hosting and use member statuses in it as a parameter for world creation.",
